---
slug: mcp-admin/reject-principal
method: post
---
{%- comment -%}
  Operator bulk-rejects EVERY pending approval for one principal (spec §9.6, §12.4).
  Complements the per-principal approval-queue cap: the cap bounds inflow, this
  drains a flooder's queue in one action instead of N reject clicks. Each rejected
  action never runs; the decision is recorded per row. Operator-gated. Bounded to the
  first 50 pending rows for the principal (the cap keeps a single principal far below
  that; a larger backlog drains over repeated clicks rather than in an unbounded loop).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  function is_admin = 'modules/mcp/commands/is_operator'
  unless is_admin
    response_status 403
    echo 'Forbidden'
    return
  endunless

  assign pid = context.params.principal_id
  if pid != blank
    assign decided_at = 'now' | to_time | strftime: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'
    graphql f = 'modules/mcp/approvals/list', status: 'pending', per_page: 50
    for a in f.records.results
      if a.principal_id == pid
        # Bulk drain: one UPDATE per pending row is inherent — mutations can't be
        # batched into a single query here. Bounded to the first 50 rows.
        # platformos-check-disable NestedGraphQLQuery
        graphql _ = 'modules/mcp/approvals/update', id: a.id, status: 'rejected', decided_by: context.current_user.id, decided_at: decided_at, result_summary: 'Bulk-rejected by operator (queue drain).'
        # platformos-check-enable NestedGraphQLQuery
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  redirect_to '/mcp-admin?tab=approvals'
-%}
